<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
    <!-- Phase 1715 — the F* model of the shared bounded fold, extracted to F#
         and compiled so the differential host can RUN it beside production
         over the conformance corpus's driver-semantics family.

         `BoundedFold.fs` is GENERATED: `proofs/check.ps1` re-extracts it from
         `proofs/BoundedFold.fst` and byte-compares the result against the
         committed copy, so editing it by hand is a change the proof leg
         refuses rather than one it absorbs. It is committed nonetheless, and
         deliberately: the F* toolchain is a large download, and requiring it
         to BUILD the repository would put a prover on the critical path of
         every contributor and every CI job that has nothing to do with proofs.
         The committed extraction is the seam — `run.ps1` compiles it like any
         other source, and the proofs job is what holds it honest.

         `IsPackable` is false and must stay false: none of this ships. The
         four packages this repository publishes carry the interpreter, not its
         model.

         Two compiler settings are forced by the extractor's output shape
         rather than chosen:

           * The strict-indentation opt-out in `OtherFlags` below. The F#
             backend emits pre-F#-8 layout (an `if ... then begin` block
             indented to its own column, a `let ... in` opening after a blank
             line). F# 8 made that an error; the flag restores it to a warning,
             and the warning is silenced below. Scoped to THIS project, so
             nothing hand-written in the repository relaxes.
           * `FS0058` (possible incorrect indentation) and `FS0064` (a type
             instantiated less generally than its annotation) off, for the same
             reason and in the same scope.

         The incomplete-match warnings the extractor's field projectors produce
         are DEMOTED rather than suppressed, and the demotion is done in the
         `Directory.Build.props` beside this file rather than here — read it for
         why the repository's FS0025 escalation is right for every file a human
         writes and not for a generated extraction, and for why it imports the
         root's settings rather than replacing them. `NoWarn` is deliberately
         NOT used: it would make the warning invisible, and it should still be
         printed and still be read. -->
    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
        <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
        <OtherFlags>$(OtherFlags) --strict-indentation-</OtherFlags>
        <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);58;64</NoWarn>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <!-- The whole runtime the extraction needs. Must precede it. -->
        <Compile Include="Prims.fs" />
        <!-- GENERATED from ../BoundedFold.fst — do not edit. A later proof
             phase APPENDS its extraction below. -->
        <Compile Include="BoundedFold.fs" />
        <!-- GENERATED from ../Budget.fst — do not edit. Phase 1716, the
             interaction budget: the saturating arithmetic, the tree walk and
             the driver's budget gate. Independent of BoundedFold above; the
             order here is the order the modules landed in. -->
        <Compile Include="Budget.fs" />
    </ItemGroup>
</Project>
